  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}). No pair verb.\n\nASPECT:\nむくんでいる indicates a current state of being swollen.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{足|あし}がむくむ (legs swell)\n・{顔|かお}がむくむ (face becomes puffy)\n・{手|て}がむくむ (hands swell)\n・{体|からだ}がむくむ (body swells)\n\nRELATED NOUN:\nむくみ - swelling, puffiness, edema\n・むくみを{取|と}る (to reduce swelling)\n・むくみ{防止|ぼうし} (swelling prevention)\n\nMEDICAL CONTEXT:\nむくみ is the common word for what is medically called {浮腫|ふしゅ} (edema). Common causes include standing for long periods, high salt intake, and poor circulation.",
